// Cloudflare Workers configuration for the live site.
//
// Two halves, one Worker:
//
//  * `/` and `/games/<slug>/` are static assets served by Cloudflare's asset
//    router. `run_worker_first` is scoped to `/api/*`, so a game page never
//    invokes a line of code — not this Worker, and not the container.
//  * `/api/*` runs the Rust service in a Cloudflare Container, reached through
//    the `ApiContainer` Durable Object (a container can only be reached through
//    its Durable Object). `edge/src/index.js` is that front door.
//
// The container instance is `lite` — a sixteenth of a vCPU, 256 MiB, 2 GB of
// disk — which the included Workers Paid allowance covers for a hobby's worth of
// play. The only CPU-bound work the service does is the argon2 hash on sign-in
// (21 ms on a full core, so a few hundred milliseconds here), and if the real
// measurement on this instance ever exceeds ~1.5 s, the fix is one word:
// `"instance_type": "basic"` (PLAN P7).
//
// The custom domain (play2learn.divanchyshyn.com) is deliberately absent: it is
// attached once in the Cloudflare dashboard, which keeps account and domain
// details out of the repository. Keeping the Worker's name `learn-and-play` is
// what keeps that domain and the `cloudflare-production` approval gate intact.
//
// Secrets are set once per Worker with `wrangler secret put` and never appear
// here: DATABASE_URL, PEPPER.
{
  "name": "learn-and-play",
  "main": "edge/src/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-20",

  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "run_worker_first": ["/api/*"]
  },

  "containers": [
    {
      "class_name": "ApiContainer",
      "image": "./api/Dockerfile",
      "instance_type": "lite",
      "max_instances": 1
    }
  ],
  "durable_objects": {
    "bindings": [{ "name": "API_CONTAINER", "class_name": "ApiContainer" }]
  },
  "exports": {
    "ApiContainer": { "type": "durable-object", "storage": "sqlite" }
  },

  "vars": {
    "PUBLIC_ORIGIN": "https://play2learn.divanchyshyn.com"
  },

  "observability": { "enabled": true }
}
